# Spec 06 Phase C — T-1 readiness gate + pace consequence (PERIPHERY)
#
# ACCEPTANCE CONTRACT (written before build)
# C1 GIVEN a persisted packing plan, WHEN its task documents are generated or the
#    move date regenerates, THEN exactly one PACKING_READINESS_GATE in-app task is
#    scheduled for moveDate−1 and ordinary packing reflow never changes that date.
# C2 GIVEN the T−1 calendar day, WHEN a new frozen dose is computed, THEN the gate
#    joins after any due packing session; before T−1 it does not join, and an
#    incomplete overdue gate remains eligible rather than being reflowed away.
# C3 GIVEN existing reserve_access_old/new workflow responses, WHEN readiness first
#    loads, THEN elevator/parking reserved is pre-filled true while the remaining
#    checklist reflects packing completion or defaults false.
# C4 GIVEN any checklist row, WHEN it is tapped, THEN all five item booleans persist
#    to users/{uid}/readiness/current; completedAt exists iff all five are true, and
#    a fresh read returns the same values.
# C5 GIVEN an incomplete gate after the T−1 calendar day ends, WHEN the card renders,
#    THEN it shows exactly one locked consequence line and does not block or loop.
# C6 GIVEN reflow requiring >1.5 remaining sessions/day, WHEN the next packing card
#    renders, THEN it shows the exact locked behind-pace nudge; an ordinary session
#    does not show that line.
# C7 GIVEN the Phase C diff, WHEN a fresh-context validator runs current-workspace
#    tests plus live iPhone/Firestore acceptance, THEN C1–C6 each receive PASS/FAIL
#    evidence and isolated fixture data is removed.
#
# NEEDS-CLARIFICATION (bounded, reversible interpretations)
# - The spec shorthand users/{uid}/readiness needs a concrete document id. Use
#   users/{uid}/readiness/current, matching packingPlan/current and identity/identity.
# - The single reservation checkbox represents every applicable RESERVE_ACCESS task:
#   prefill true when every generated old/new access task has a nonempty corresponding
#   workflow response; if task docs are absent but a response exists, response presence
#   is the safe backward-compatible signal. No reservation vendor semantics are invented.
# - "At day's end" means from the start of move day onward (the first instant after
#   the moveDate−1 calendar day). The warning is display-only; the gate remains usable.
# - Readiness is scheduled work in addition to the at-most-one packing-session rule.
#   On T−1 it follows the packing session so the first-night bag can be completed first.
#
